WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.085
The finale of the
second series of Outer Banks

00:00:02.169 --> 00:00:04.254
comes with
a whole load of twists,

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:05.464
as you've come to expect

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:07.257
from
this adventure mystery show

00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:09.051
starring our favourite
runaway pogues.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.136
We got it!

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.681
So much happened
this season.

00:00:15.182 --> 00:00:16.892
John B went from fugitive

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:17.851
to prisoner

00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:19.269
to exonerated man.

00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:21.355
Oh, you know
they can't keep me in, boy!

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:23.565
Pope found out
his family heirloom is

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:25.234
a giant golden cross.

00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:26.401
We did it!

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:28.695
And Kiara got kicked out
by her parents.

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:30.239
Go live
like a fricking pogue!

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:32.407
But let's get to some
of the twists and turns

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:33.575
of the final few episodes

00:00:33.659 --> 00:00:35.536
and dig into
what they reveal

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:38.539
and what they set up for
the pogues in the future.

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:41.792
Let's start with the first.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:42.793
Mid-season,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.754
Ward Cameron appears to die
aboard his ship

00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:47.214
after setting off
an explosion

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:50.008
and admitting to
all of his misdeeds.

00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:50.968
I did it.

00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:56.306
I did all of it.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.349
Crucially,

00:00:57.432 --> 00:01:00.018
he also takes the fall
for shooting the sheriff.

00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:02.604
Of course, as Sarah
and John B witnessed,

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:04.773
it was actually Rafe
who murdered her.

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:06.817
Not the first
or the last time

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.193
he tries to murder someone
on this show,

00:01:08.277 --> 00:01:10.362
yet only the pogues seem to
see him

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:11.864
as what he really is.

00:01:12.364 --> 00:01:13.490
-We know what you did!
-Hey.

00:01:13.574 --> 00:01:15.367
-Murderer!
-No.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:18.036
Speaking of things not being
what they seem,

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.038
there was definitely
something fishy

00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:21.331
about Mr. Cameron's death.

00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:24.793
And it turns out
he faked his death

00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:26.128
in a bid to escape

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:28.714
and to ensure Rafe
didn't see prison time.

00:01:29.298 --> 00:01:31.175
It's the only way to be
a family again.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:34.845
He ends the series
still very much alive,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.805
despite a run-in
with John B.

00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:40.934
While John B seemed to
have the chance

00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:43.562
to end the war between them
once and for all,

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.565
with eerie mirroring of how
Ward dealt with his father,

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:48.567
more on that later,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.652
he decides to
take the higher ground

00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:52.321
and spare
Mr. Cameron's life.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:54.489
So, now we wonder:

00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:57.284
will Ward Cameron's bid
for freedom at sea work

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.995
or will the cops realise
he's still alive?

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:01.872
Now, last season,

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.582
the drama all hinged
on the treasure

00:02:03.665 --> 00:02:04.875
aboard the Royal Merchant.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:08.295
With that treasure found…
and lost,

00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:10.589
there's a gap for a new hunt
on the horizon.

00:02:11.548 --> 00:02:13.759
When Pope gets a strange
letter from a rich lady

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:16.261
demanding to know
the location of a key,

00:02:16.345 --> 00:02:18.388
a new mystery is afoot.

00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:21.558
And it turns out Pope's
family was more involved

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:24.728
with the Royal Merchant than
any of them ever realised.

00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:27.064
Here lies Denmark Tanny:

00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:29.525
the famous ex-slave.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.819
Denmark and Cecilia

00:02:34.363 --> 00:02:37.074
Are your great grandfolks
going way back.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.785
They eventually find
Denmark Tanny's cross

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.370
in a dilapidated church.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.123
Unfortunately, after Pope
goes into anaphylactic shock

00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:46.583
due to wasp stings,

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:49.253
forcing them to abandon the
treasure for medical help,

00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:50.420
so does Rafe Cameron.

00:02:50.504 --> 00:02:53.090
He, in turn, brings it
aboard the ship

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.384
carrying our old friend
Ward Cameron.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:56.426
At this point,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:58.762
the final battle
upon the coastal venture

00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:00.681
is not just one
for the cross,

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:01.807
but for Pope's heritage.

00:03:02.641 --> 00:03:04.059
The time
where people do shit to us

00:03:04.142 --> 00:03:06.728
and we just sit back
and take it is over!

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:08.146
That's my boy!

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.566
Thanks to help
from their old friend Cleo,

00:03:10.649 --> 00:03:12.776
they get so close
to their goal.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.362
At one point, Pope
is willing to let the cross

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:16.405
drop into the ocean

00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:18.365
rather than
let the Camerons have it.

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:20.617
If we can't have it,
no one can.

00:03:22.077 --> 00:03:23.203
Sorry, Denmark.

00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:24.788
Unfortunately,

00:03:24.872 --> 00:03:27.332
Rafe and the crew manage to
drag it back aboard

00:03:27.416 --> 00:03:28.667
while Pope
and his friends watch

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.419
from
their departing speedboat.

00:03:30.502 --> 00:03:31.879
It's safe to say, however,

00:03:31.962 --> 00:03:34.214
the search for the cross
transformed Pope,

00:03:34.798 --> 00:03:36.466
so it's not likely
he'll let them take it

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.177
without a fight
to get it back.

00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:39.887
This shit ain't over.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:42.848
The pogues, along with
adoptees Cleo and Sarah,

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:45.100
end up on a seemingly
abandoned island

00:03:45.184 --> 00:03:46.310
somewhere in the Caribbean

00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:49.229
and decide to stay put to
live their best pogue life.

00:03:49.313 --> 00:03:51.190
I claim thee Poguelandia.

00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:54.067
I like the ring of it.
I'm going to make a flag.

00:03:54.151 --> 00:03:55.319
It's going to have a chicken
on it.

00:03:55.402 --> 00:03:58.113
With a coconut bra,
smoking a J.

00:03:58.197 --> 00:03:59.072
And crocs.

00:03:59.156 --> 00:04:00.532
Back on the outer banks,

00:04:00.616 --> 00:04:03.076
their family and friends
have reported them missing,

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:06.288
so exactly how much trouble
are they going to be in

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:07.372
upon their return?

00:04:07.873 --> 00:04:10.751
There's one final mystery
unveiled in the finale.

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:13.420
Limbrey, the rich woman
obsessed with

00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:14.796
finding Denmark's cross,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.548
knocks on a stranger's door.

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:18.217
And that stranger?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.302
Well, it's only Big John,

00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:22.054
a.k.a. John B's dad.

00:04:22.554 --> 00:04:24.264
He seems to have been there
for a while

00:04:24.348 --> 00:04:25.724
from the conversation
Limbrey has

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:26.767
with his caretaker.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:27.851
How is he?

00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:29.937
Half dead.

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:31.980
For a long time.

00:04:32.064 --> 00:04:34.149
Just like John B found
plenty of notes

00:04:34.233 --> 00:04:35.234
about the Royal Merchant

00:04:35.317 --> 00:04:36.693
in his father's
abandoned office

00:04:36.777 --> 00:04:37.903
in season one,

00:04:37.986 --> 00:04:40.197
Limbrey takes a peek
around his makeshift office

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.406
in this new home

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.576
with coordinates written
everywhere in red ink.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.788
Unsurprisingly, Limbrey is
there about the shroud

00:04:47.871 --> 00:04:50.123
she believed to be hidden
in Denmark's cross

00:04:50.207 --> 00:04:52.251
and Big John seems to
know all about it,

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.837
but his information
comes at a cost.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.296
I know where it is.

00:04:57.464 --> 00:04:58.340
I can help you.

00:05:01.969 --> 00:05:02.928
But you…

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.556
have to help my son.

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:09.309
This cliff hanger leaves us
with so many questions,

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:12.896
namely:
How did Big John survive?

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:13.981
Who rescued him?

00:05:14.064 --> 00:05:16.275
Is John B going to
find out about this?

00:05:16.358 --> 00:05:18.277
And how is he going to feel
about it?

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.113
And how will Pope feel
about this unlikely team

00:05:21.196 --> 00:05:23.740
comprising of his friend's
supposedly deceased father

00:05:23.824 --> 00:05:25.284
and a woman
who tried to kill him

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:26.702
for his family's treasure?

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.538
Well, if news
of a season three drops,

00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:30.789
you'll know
where to find us.

00:05:31.498 --> 00:05:32.499
Until then…

00:05:33.083 --> 00:05:34.418
Welcome back
to the pogue life.

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:35.460
Full pogue.

00:05:35.544 --> 00:05:36.587
Full pogue!

